{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T23:51:11.145764Z","id":"9244d41bcac0a23b520e655ecbd9fd2e98c2ea1f31cde4189c075fd84bdd171a","body":{"detail":"signedFetch signs t = now()/1000 from the injected clock (Date.now by default). The daemon refuses a t more than MAX_SKEW_S (120 s, crates/clax-core/src/sig.rs) from its clock, so a reporter whose machine clock is off by more than two minutes has every call refused. plugins/pi/src/remote.ts learns an offset from the response Date header; a cross-origin page cannot read Date unless the reporter routes expose it (Access-Control-Expose-Headers: date). ReporterClient's renewal also compares the local clock with the server's expires_at.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":56},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"e1bc170eec17688fc16899fa33b17fda9db0ce1a94df938770166fb24e633804"},"suggested_fix":"Expose Date on the reporter routes' CORS answers and learn an offset as learnOffset in plugins/pi/src/remote.ts does; or have a stale-time error carry the server time.","summary":"Signed requests use the page's own clock for t, with no learned offset","tags":["review","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T23:51:11.145835Z","id":"51ddfaae32e0c17bb230b724cf8768b4d8717539605ed06d912517b7a1aff153","body":{"detail":"ReporterClient makes a non-extractable WebCrypto key per client instance (generateSigner) unless one is passed as signer. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md §5.1 keeps a browser's key in IndexedDB. A reporter token lives 15 minutes and is bound to the key, so a fresh key per page load costs one auth call per load and nothing else.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"6a70b6f96b89c147e21d292528c4426e4dbf65ef6810f5cb6720bfea97963a2c"},"summary":"Reporter key kept in memory, not in IndexedDB","tags":["revisit:a deployer needs reporter tokens to survive page reloads, or auth calls per load become a cost","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T23:51:11.145863Z","id":"1c4e7fceccdde766c2fcd075141caabad32b2797e633e7f4b99bcac3c5287c62","body":{"detail":"The plan's route table (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-27-report-queues-m1.md, Shared shapes) lists the multipart fields external_id?, url, title, anchor, body, metadata?, revision?, clip? without saying how anchor and metadata are encoded. ReporterClient.fileReport sends each as JSON.stringify of the value, and the clip as a part named clip with filename clip.png and type image/png. The reporter route in crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_reporter.rs must parse the same; until a test files a report through this client against the real route (the browser test planned in Task 8), the two can disagree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"5fb25e7605a124933d130dc5d11e0d42052cd9367942b01da4eb034bf0d6d23c"},"summary":"fileReport sends anchor and metadata as JSON text in multipart fields","tags":["review","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/types.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:03:57.029346Z","id":"8e0d5e0aac12c292760e5cbfdbe086d5df5c1eefa7c605b56ba9ddba8e1a4855","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-http/src/error.rs IntoResponse for ApiError builds json!({\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\", ...extra}}). The shell's callers (web/shell/src/queues/api.ts, web/shell/src/people/api.ts) read error.code and error.message.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":114},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"0d54957595793dbf7f01aeea3f18d290baa9d17a5615c64aa2e724232f1a91ec"},"suggested_fix":"Type it as {error: {code: string; message: string}} and read it that way in the SDK's client.","summary":"ApiErrorBody types the error answer as {error: string, message: string}, but the daemon answers {error: {code, message}}","tags":["queues","sdk","interface","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/types.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:06:12.103841Z","id":"4e205dcf32a2dba629a6ab146031fb47a4ef44157b536e1fef60662047e1c56d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:13d7bfb0e","summary":"ApiErrorBody is now {error: {code, message}} as ApiError answers (crates/clax-http/src/error.rs:311-314); failure() reads error.code; bazel test //web:unit PASSED","supersedes":"8e0d5e0aac12c292760e5cbfdbe086d5df5c1eefa7c605b56ba9ddba8e1a4855","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/diagnostics.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T07:01:58.638723Z","id":"bffff2952b964fe2df2b39c3185031ce428ff3397d65c71504554efad83b050d","body":{"detail":"record() in web/sdk/src/diagnostics.ts applies scrub() to every line's text, as parse_diagnostics in crates/clax-core/src/report.rs does on receipt. scrub() replaces the values of secret keys (token=, key=, password=, …), credentials, emails and long runs, but not the value of an ordinary query key: console.error('load failed https://app.example/search?q=alice+smith') is kept as written. Only the request lines (kind request) and an error event's filename go through scrubUrl().","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"73012337fb1bca264c9cb21526d976b66383084488ba67dbe26b5fbc515d04be"},"suggested_fix":"Add a rule to scrub.rs (and the shared table web/sdk/test/scrub-cases.json) that scrubUrl()s each scheme://… run inside free text, then port it to web/sdk/src/scrub.ts.","summary":"Diagnostics text is scrub()bed, not scrubUrl()ed: a URL inside a console message or stack keeps its non-secret query values","tags":["sdk","privacy","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T07:24:32.758801Z","id":"291630c80bd5e5571e3cb33a4277bf46fcd8290ff89e0ccd6fa0327b0e714ad8","body":{"detail":"The plan's route table (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-27-report-queues-m1.md, Shared shapes) lists the multipart fields external_id?, url, title, anchor, body, metadata?, revision?, clip? without saying how anchor and metadata are encoded. ReporterClient.fileReport sends each as JSON.stringify of the value, and the clip as a part named clip with filename clip.png and type image/png. The reporter route in crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_reporter.rs must parse the same; until a test files a report through this client against the real route (the browser test planned in Task 8), the two can disagree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"26846850bbb5874aabaab6402cc0c53b7d96ee1001bb28d920647d19db9e2e4d"},"summary":"fileReport sends anchor and metadata as JSON text in multipart fields","supersedes":"1c4e7fceccdde766c2fcd075141caabad32b2797e633e7f4b99bcac3c5287c62","tags":["review","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T07:24:32.847089Z","id":"31807e56f1b2be194c64ec655f44f4e76fb0fedc749d08f4b43c387fdcd5f449","body":{"detail":"ReporterClient makes a non-extractable WebCrypto key per client instance (generateSigner) unless one is passed as signer. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md §5.1 keeps a browser's key in IndexedDB. A reporter token lives 15 minutes and is bound to the key, so a fresh key per page load costs one auth call per load and nothing else.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"181a84e5a0f9368d0dadebe200b43a30843568418ae40ac573d0a3d9ef958850"},"summary":"Reporter key kept in memory, not in IndexedDB","supersedes":"51ddfaae32e0c17bb230b724cf8768b4d8717539605ed06d912517b7a1aff153","tags":["revisit:a deployer needs reporter tokens to survive page reloads, or auth calls per load become a cost","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/diagnostics.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T07:24:32.941395Z","id":"3c6ed3c0f93bb2ad79c3ea335a145676f43f4b8861c65d3720aa418e137e59ae","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a19cedcce","span":{"start":{"line":89},"end":{"line":97},"content_hash":"a599ba8b0c4f3cec1dd933a6c2bd4614b21c2effdd0770c5a0b0bcd8c043a4b3"},"summary":"scrub() in crates/clax-core/src/scrub.rs (module doc, url_at) and web/sdk/src/scrub.ts (urlAt) now gives every http:// or https:// URL inside a scrubbed text its scrub_url form, so console text and stacks lose ordinary query values; shared rows added to web/sdk/test/scrub-cases.json ('load failed https://app.example/search?q=alice+smith&page=2 retrying' -> q and page redacted). bazel test //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test //web:unit PASSED.","supersedes":"bffff2952b964fe2df2b39c3185031ce428ff3397d65c71504554efad83b050d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/diagnostics.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:38:04.587356Z","id":"8a996dfa987707b683e79aacf02ee735a8097bef0ba4ece2a5f6f1d1e36706b3","body":{"detail":"The overlay starts the recorder with `{instance}` (web/overlay/src/main.ts, `installDiagnostics(win, { instance })`), and `skipped` drops every request to that origin. For the Clax shell (web/shell/src/feedback/feedback.ts, startFeedback) the instance is location.origin, so a failing `/api/...` call of the shell never becomes a diagnostics line; only console lines, errors and rejections are kept. The SDK's own reporter calls are already skipped by their `Clax-Signature` header, so the origin rule only adds the unsigned overlay.js load and the host's own token route.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":88},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"176fd2c8d63146d1de04796cd727f975f78e70f2ea1127ac75ee15b00a6992bc"},"suggested_fix":"Skip the instance's reporter routes (`/api/queues/<qid>/reporter/...`) and overlay files by path rather than the whole origin, or let the host pass `diagnostics: {skipInstance: false}`; add a test where the instance is the page's origin and a failed same-origin `/api/x` is recorded.","summary":"On an instance that is its own integrating product (clax.dev), the instance origin is the page's own origin, so every same-origin request of the page goes unrecorded","tags":["review","feedback-loop","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/diagnostics.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T16:11:41.905988Z","id":"03869cf1e420f188e749579097c353e8b663a186f8a4384ae3f2163266336a8f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:81d77e09b","summary":"The recorder now skips only the SDK's own traffic to an instance (SDK_PATH: `/_clax/` and `/api/queues/<qid>/reporter...`) plus signed requests. web/sdk/src/diagnostics.test.ts 'records a page's own requests when the instance is the page's own origin, but not the SDK's' (instance https://app.example = page origin: GET /api/x and /api/queues/q1/reports recorded; /_clax/overlay.js, /reporter/badge, /reporter-tokens not) passes: bazel test //web:unit PASSED (target/fr1-green2.log).","supersedes":"8a996dfa987707b683e79aacf02ee735a8097bef0ba4ece2a5f6f1d1e36706b3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T16:37:05.453149Z","id":"78061ced5f9a211b49a5b17e748197f9edbaa3827bd574e84cad353f60abe24c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0af758fbd","summary":"Its revisit condition came true and was acted on: with ReporterOptions.user (the overlay's user) the client keeps its key, a non-extractable CryptoKey, and its token in IndexedDB per instance, queue and user (web/sdk/src/keystore.ts), forgets them on sign-out (ReporterClient.forget, Clax.forgetReporter), and keeps them in memory alone without a user or where IndexedDB fails. Tests: web/sdk/src/keystore.test.ts under //web:unit.","supersedes":"31807e56f1b2be194c64ec655f44f4e76fb0fedc749d08f4b43c387fdcd5f449","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:57.090593Z","id":"e43afc42717197a52a704cf02774c5840a38a214b5a20686660b664c29692ad3","body":{"detail":"The plan's route table (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-27-report-queues-m1.md, Shared shapes) lists the multipart fields external_id?, url, title, anchor, body, metadata?, revision?, clip? without saying how anchor and metadata are encoded. ReporterClient.fileReport sends each as JSON.stringify of the value, and the clip as a part named clip with filename clip.png and type image/png. The reporter route in crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_reporter.rs must parse the same; until a test files a report through this client against the real route (the browser test planned in Task 8), the two can disagree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"698e79ba112f19722cc1f3fc5c0ba1ba275c227fea2a7dc63e99acb71fa6c721"},"summary":"fileReport sends anchor and metadata as JSON text in multipart fields","supersedes":"291630c80bd5e5571e3cb33a4277bf46fcd8290ff89e0ccd6fa0327b0e714ad8","tags":["review","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/diagnostics.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:56:47.896391Z","id":"b5a011b1b591b80f33ec787d8a678b71c77a573c18580e8a1b7d21b8777dea79","body":{"detail":"Two copies on one page are expected: /_clax/overlay.js bundles its own copy at Clax's version (web/vite.overlay.config.ts), and an app that also installs @empathic/clax-client-sdk carries another at the package's own version. installDiagnostics() (line 86) returns whatever recorder another copy left at `win[Symbol.for(\"clax.diagnostics\")]` (line 68) and calls `existing.ignore(...)` on it (line 90). `ignore` is on the internal `Installed` interface (line 57), not on the public `Recorder`. So a later SDK that renames or drops `ignore`, or changes what `lines()` returns, makes overlay() throw a TypeError, or file malformed diagnostics, on any page where the other copy installed first. The keystore's IndexedDB database (web/sdk/src/keystore.ts) is shared the same way, with no versionchange handling.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":57},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"e7249c1b0708cfa96bc083ae08f9170376d130140c52b95b0e451ee73a2b0a92"},"suggested_fix":"Treat both as cross-version protocols. Store `{ v: 1, recorder }` under the symbol, and have a copy that finds an unknown `v`, or a missing method, start a recorder of its own instead of calling into the other. Put `ignore` on the public Recorder contract, or check for it before calling. Close the database on `versionchange` in indexedDbStore().","summary":"Copies of the SDK at different versions on one page share an unversioned recorder object under Symbol.for(\"clax.diagnostics\"), and an unversioned IndexedDB store, and call each other's internal methods","tags":["review","review:pr45-client-split","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:37:27.481395Z","id":"eea1d225c9a144b5627fc6dfc9a48139ea819d2b4c77adeb919ce9a76c3088ef","body":{"detail":"send() treats any 401 as an expired token: it drops the token, calls the deployer's auth (one mint, signed by the queue's single service-grant key) and resends once. The reporter routes also answer 401 for refusals that have nothing to do with the token: stale_request (t more than 120 s from the instance's clock, crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs refuse(), status UNAUTHORIZED for every SigError but Full), replayed_request and invalid_signature (for example a proxy that rewrites Host or the path, both of which the signature covers). In each case the retry fails the same way, so every call from that browser costs an extra mint. docs/feedback.md ('What the token route sees') says every mint shares the grant key's 1,024 requests per 240 s across the whole product, so one misconfigured proxy or a population of skewed clocks (the overlay polls the badge every minute and on focus) spends the product-wide mint budget and starts 429 limit_reached for everyone. The clock-skew offset itself is a separate open concern on web/sdk/src/client.ts:56:62 (record 9244d41b); this one is about which 401s should trigger a re-mint.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"4ae7065b09af9f6e70e432728f6338473d7b8c03cb3c838d2428a86ee9c4f3df"},"suggested_fix":"Re-mint and resend only on 401 token_expired or invalid_token (read the error body's code before deciding); answer stale_request, replayed_request and invalid_signature as a ClaxError at once (re-signing with a fresh nonce for replayed_request, and with a learned offset for stale_request once 9244d41b is addressed). Add a reporter.test.ts case asserting that a 401 stale_request calls auth once in total.","summary":"ReporterClient re-mints a token on every 401, including stale_request, replayed_request and invalid_signature, which a new token cannot fix","tags":["review","review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:37:27.481450Z","id":"476007f9757cb68398efe61c40f6c2205af7afd0910454fbb1ff6befb6f303c9","body":{"detail":"docs/contract.md 'Signed requests' says the clients 'retry limit_reached and busy three times, after 1, 2 and 4 seconds with jitter, re-signing each', and docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md section 4.1 puts retries in the client core. web/sdk does neither: failure() builds a ClaxError of code, message and status only, so a caller cannot read the Retry-After that docs/feedback.md ('What the token route sees') promises with every 429 limit_reached, and ServiceClient.mintReporterToken and every ReporterClient call fail on the first 429. In a browser the header could not be read anyway: the reporter routes' CORS layer (crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs cors(), lines 348-387) sets Access-Control-Allow-Origin but no Access-Control-Expose-Headers, and Retry-After is not a CORS-safelisted response header. The TypeScript backend in docs/feedback.md (lines 136-144) passes limit_reached back to the browser with e.status but cannot pass its Retry-After, unlike clax.dev's own route, which docs/contract.md (the /_app/feedback/token row) says answers 429 'with its Retry-After'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":93},"end":{"line":101},"content_hash":"4acc88017a52ac21ffdb9a3e4e2908dbf2c949360c04a14902df87a21e5f17c3"},"suggested_fix":"Give ClaxError a retryAfterS (from Retry-After, or the body's retry_after_s where an error carries one); retry limit_reached and busy in signedFetch's callers as the contract says, re-signing each attempt; add `Access-Control-Expose-Headers: retry-after, date` to the reporter routes' CORS answers in crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs (and the Worker's twin); and show the backend snippet in docs/feedback.md forwarding Retry-After.","summary":"The SDK neither retries 429 limit_reached / 503 busy nor exposes Retry-After, though the contract and the SDK design say clients do","tags":["review","review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:37:27.481635Z","id":"aa31af465ddf6d4e862217ee22d93b157ac447ddbe53533eb431315b6db36531","body":{"detail":"signedFetch resolves `new URL(r.path, r.instance)` with a path starting with '/', so `instance: \"https://apps.example.com/clax\"` sends to https://apps.example.com/api/queues/..., dropping /clax with no error, and the overlay's /_clax/ files resolve the same way. The server cannot serve under a prefix anyway: the fleet routes by Host (docs/kubernetes.md, How it scales) and the signature covers the path as the instance receives it, so an Ingress that strips a prefix breaks every signature with 401 invalid_signature. Nothing in web/sdk/README.md, docs/feedback.md or the `instance` doc comments (reporter.ts:21-22, service.ts:10-11) says `instance` must be an origin, so a deployer who mounts Clax under a path gets requests to the wrong place or a 401 that, through ReporterClient's 401 retry, also re-mints.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"4adcfe8c5a144e7aebdf2720728b3648d4590c66113872b116503627b1206c57"},"suggested_fix":"Have ReporterClient, ServiceClient and overlay() throw a TypeError when `instance` has a path other than '/', a query or a fragment ('instance must be an origin, such as https://clax.example.com'), and say in the option docs that Clax is served at the root of its own host.","summary":"An `instance` with a path (an instance behind a path prefix) is silently reduced to its origin","tags":["review","review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/types.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:37:27.481668Z","id":"a44caed53580e8d9911415e68575a7f97acbb3c6a130254397d4e028a5391c53","body":{"detail":"The exported QueueErrorCode lists lease_lost, thread_taken, external_artifact, wrong_origin, token_expired, not_a_member, not_fix_proposed, not_claimable and five invalid_* codes. The routes the SDK calls also answer invalid_token, invalid_signature, stale_request, replayed_request, limit_reached, forbidden_origin, invalid_key, invalid_args, body_too_large, busy, timeout and not_found (crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs ServiceCaller/ReporterCaller doc comments; docs/contract.md 'Signed requests'), plus the SDK's own network, bad_response and unsupported_browser (client.ts, reporter.ts). docs/feedback.md's backend snippet switches on invalid_key and limit_reached, neither in the type, so a consumer who narrows ClaxError.code to QueueErrorCode gets no help for the codes that matter.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":296},"end":{"line":310},"content_hash":"8995d25c34f578882c6a52e88bead38cfd7976bae06cd564cb089326a3fe4e7f"},"suggested_fix":"List every code those routes and the SDK answer in QueueErrorCode (or a ClaxErrorCode union used as ClaxError.code's type, widened with `string & {}`), and test the list against the server's codes as the contract test does for routes.","summary":"QueueErrorCode omits most codes the reporter and service routes answer","tags":["review","review:k8s-day-two-2026-11-02","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:41:07.376298Z","id":"217f0a95ecb3d4c906d56b687d9cce3e6b8357ecdbcc8d05c96d0cc8923813d6","body":{"detail":"web/sdk/src/reporter.ts:337-341: `if (first.status !== 401) return first; this.token = undefined; ... return once((await this.current()).token);` reads no error code. crates/clax-http/src/grant_auth.rs:714-729 refuse() answers StatusCode::UNAUTHORIZED for SigError::Stale, Replayed and Bad (only Full is 429), and the reporter routes use it (crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs:167, 171, 196, 201; doc comment at 220-221 lists 401 invalid_signature, stale_request, replayed_request). A fresh token changes none of those inputs (clock, Host, path), so the resend fails the same way after one extra mint. docs/feedback.md:291-300 states every mint is signed by the one grant key, capped at 1,024 per 240 s. docs/contract.md:4494-4495 does describe re-asking 'after a 401', so the fix also needs that sentence narrowed. Kind concern is right: a risk under misconfiguration or clock skew, not a pre-merge defect.","kind":"comment","references":"eea1d225c9a144b5627fc6dfc9a48139ea819d2b4c77adeb919ce9a76c3088ef","summary":"confirmed: send() drops the token and calls auth again on any 401, whatever its code","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:41:07.376783Z","id":"cae869e7f6633ff1f2aeb740a83b6c1e8614c9df06fce0336cd7af869d732997","body":{"detail":"web/sdk/src/client.ts:10-15 ClaxError carries code, message and status only; client.ts:93-101 failure() reads only the JSON body; `grep -n etry web/sdk/src/*.ts` (non-test) finds no retry loop. `grep -rni expose-headers crates/ web/sdk web/overlay docs/contract.md` finds nothing outside .qual files; crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs:348-387 cors() sets Allow-Origin (and preflight Allow-Methods/Headers/Max-Age) only, so a cross-origin page cannot read Retry-After or Date. docs/feedback.md:298 promises Retry-After with every 429 limit_reached, and docs/feedback.md:136-141 forwards only code and status. One nuance: the 'retry limit_reached and busy three times' sentence (docs/contract.md:6042-6045) sits in '### Signed requests' under 'People and their agents' (Clax-Grant clients), not in 'Report queue routes', so the obligation on web/sdk is by analogy and via the SDK design spec section 4.1 ('retries ... in the client core'); the gap the record names is real either way. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"476007f9757cb68398efe61c40f6c2205af7afd0910454fbb1ff6befb6f303c9","summary":"confirmed: no retry of limit_reached/busy, no Retry-After on ClaxError, and no Access-Control-Expose-Headers on the reporter routes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:41:07.379548Z","id":"9e19caf5e6acc75fd8ea29862c27f1801d738c99bd12cadec204b731ce8e252c","body":{"detail":"web/sdk/src/client.ts:54 `new URL(r.path, r.instance)` with r.path from queuePath() (client.ts:46-48, always '/api/queues/...'). `node -e 'console.log(new URL(\"/api/queues/q\", \"https://apps.example.com/clax\").href)'` prints https://apps.example.com/api/queues/q. Neither web/sdk/src/reporter.ts:21-22 ('The instance's base URL') nor service.ts:9-10 nor web/overlay/src/main.ts:107-111 (which only strips trailing slashes) rejects or documents a path. One sub-claim is overstated: the overlay fetches no /_clax/ file at runtime (`grep -rn _clax web/overlay/src` matches only comments), so only the API calls are affected. Kind suggestion is right.","kind":"comment","references":"aa31af465ddf6d4e862217ee22d93b157ac447ddbe53533eb431315b6db36531","summary":"confirmed: signedFetch drops any path in `instance` without an error","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/sdk/src/types.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T03:41:07.380018Z","id":"3477ff165f43b6e541f6b27a062eb84bbcc83af628a51c80959c22495f6cfc91","body":{"detail":"web/sdk/src/types.ts:296-309 lists lease_lost, thread_taken, external_artifact, wrong_origin, token_expired, not_a_member, not_fix_proposed, not_claimable, invalid_context, invalid_diagnostics, invalid_profile, invalid_fix, invalid_query. crates/clax-http/src/reporter.rs:220-221 and 287-288 document 401 invalid_signature, stale_request, replayed_request and 429 limit_reached; docs/contract.md:6028-6041 adds invalid_token, forbidden_origin, body_too_large, busy, timeout; docs/feedback.md:139 switches on invalid_key and limit_reached. `grep -rn QueueErrorCode web/sdk/src web/overlay/src` finds only the declaration, so nothing ties it to ClaxError.code (a string, client.ts:11). Kind suggestion is right.","kind":"comment","references":"a44caed53580e8d9911415e68575a7f97acbb3c6a130254397d4e028a5391c53","summary":"confirmed: QueueErrorCode lists 13 codes and omits invalid_key, limit_reached, stale_request and the other codes the SDK's routes answer","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:6339925b-eee1-47c9-bafb-ab7115d6c4da"]}}
